## Dependency and invalidation decision

Every mapping binds the exact source hash, field-set hash, transform policy, and relevant native contract. Stock-bound projections also depend on the V5 scope pin and selected stock/preparation receipts; evidence-bound projections depend on operation-scoped rights and accepted B1 extraction; qualification outputs depend on current engine, adapter, configuration, and seed hashes.

Inventory-only changes invalidate inventory/build projections, not independently bound target ancestry, source evidence, physical measurements, empirical OAV, or observations. A source or transform change invalidates its descendants unless a typed, tested semantic-equivalence rule proves invariance. Unchanged aggregate counts are never equivalence evidence. No standalone dependency DAG or invalidation truth store is justified at P2.2.

## Migration and authority verdict

- Native overlap is substantial; reuse is mandatory.
- No new schema or migration is proven by this six-source diff.
- If a future real persistence gap is demonstrated, an additive migration must descend from `20260810_0016`.
- The known missing typed sensory-assurance slice remains a separate future design gap; these package fields do not authorize reconstructing it.
- No package `physically_authorized` value, unknown stock strength, float active-lineage value, proxy OAV, dose-firewall heuristic, package gate, or reference result is promoted.
- Canonical import and project installation remain unauthorized at this gate.

